# ErrorLogger (Turtle WoW Addon)

## 📌 Overview
ErrorLogger is a lightweight Turtle WoW addon that automatically captures Lua errors from **macros and addons**, logs them to your SavedVariables, and makes them viewable in-game or after logout.

This helps you debug your custom addons and macros without missing hidden errors.

---

## 🚀 Installation
1. Download / copy the `ErrorLogger` folder into your WoW directory:
World of Warcraft\Interface\AddOns\ErrorLogger

yaml
Copy code
2. Restart the game and enable **ErrorLogger** in the AddOns menu on the character select screen.

---

## 🔧 Features
- Forces script errors to be enabled (`/console scriptErrors 1`).
- Saves every error to `SavedVariables` (`ErrorLoggerDB`).
- Prints error messages to chat in red.
- Command `/errors` shows the last 5 logged errors.

---

## 📂 Saved Data
All logged errors are saved here:
WTF\Account<YourAccountName>\SavedVariables\ErrorLogger.lua



Each entry has a timestamp and the error message.

---

## 📜 Commands
- `/errors` → Shows the last 5 logged errors in your chat frame.

---

## ✅ Example
If an addon throws an error:
Interface\AddOns\SomeAddon\file.lua:123: attempt to index a nil value


You’ll see:
[ErrorLogger] Interface\AddOns\SomeAddon\file.lua:123: attempt to index a nil value



And it will be saved to your log file for later inspection.

